{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3043","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3043","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3043\",\"parent_revision\":\"0475b7afdac8ebbf681eb1b8be251157368894e7e9633a94fcc38ac8a11a7119\",\"root_revision\":\"0475b7afdac8ebbf681eb1b8be251157368894e7e9633a94fcc38ac8a11a7119\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## What And Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPR #3042 fixed 20 pre-existing files on `main` whose PEP 723 shebang used\\n`#!/usr/bin/env -S uv --quiet run --active --script` instead of this repo's\\ncanonical `#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script`\\n(see `.claude/rules/script-invocation.md`). The `--active` flag makes `uv run`\\nreuse and mutate the shared project `.venv` with the script's own PEP 723\\ndependencies instead of resolving an isolated ephemeral environment \u2014 the\\nopposite of what a self-contained, standalone PEP 723 script needs, and a\\nrisk of dependency-version collisions across unrelated scripts sharing one\\n`.venv`.\\n\\nA repo-wide grep during that work turned up **41 more files** with the exact\\nsame bug, deliberately left untouched in #3042 because they were outside its\\nstated 20-file scope. Re-run this to regenerate the current list (it will\\ndrift as files move):\\n\\n```\\ngrep -rln \\\"uv --quiet run --active --script\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" .\\n```\\n\\nAs of PR #3042 (2026-08-20), the list included files under:\\n- `.claude/skills/create-merge-request-changelog/scripts/`\\n- `.claude/skills/daily-releases/scripts/`\\n- `.claude/skills/gh/scripts/`\\n- `.claude/skills/session-historian/scripts/`\\n- `.claude/utilities/find-temp-documentation.py`\\n- `examples/solid-review-ab/runner/cli.py`\\n- `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/cli.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/{monitor,spawn}.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/run_pytest.py`\\n- `plugins/frustration-analyzer/mcp/server.py`\\n- `plugins/gitlab-skill/skills/gitlab-skill/scripts/`\\n- `plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting/scripts/`\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-cli/assets/` (several)\\n- `plugins/python3-development/skills/typer-and-rich/assets/` (several \u2014 likely\\n  duplicates of the python-engineering ones above)\\n- `plugins/rtfp/skills/rtfp/scripts/`\\n</div>\\n\\n## A More Consequential Related Bug\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/python3-development/scripts/validate_pep723.py` \u2014 the script that is\\npresumably meant to *validate* shebang correctness \u2014 has the identical buggy\\nstring baked into its own \\\"canonical\\\" reference:\\n\\n- Line 47: `UV_SHEBANG = \\\"#!/usr/bin/env -S uv --quiet run --active --script\\\"`\\n- Line 330: a docstring example showing the same wrong pattern\\n\\nThis means the repo's own shebang validator currently teaches/accepts the\\nwrong pattern. This is a plausible root cause for why the bug spread to 61+\\nfiles across the repo, and should likely be fixed **before** or **alongside**\\nsweeping the remaining 41 files, so the validator doesn't immediately flag\\nthe corrected files as wrong (or silently accept regressions back to\\n`--active`).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis item intentionally excludes PR #3042's 20 already-fixed files. It also\\nexcludes PR #2787 / branch `codex-plugin-usability-port`, where Copilot's\\nreview originally surfaced this pattern for 2 in-diff files (already fixed\\nthere) \u2014 this whole shebang-drift thread started as an out-of-scope\\nobservation during that PR's review.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Approach\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Fix `validate_pep723.py`'s `UV_SHEBANG` constant and docstring first (single\\n   file, low risk, likely closes the root cause).\\n2. Re-run the grep above to get the current file list (it may differ from the\\n   2026-08-20 snapshot).\\n3. Apply the same line-1-only shebang fix pattern used in PR #3042, verified\\n   file-by-file (`Read` before `Edit`, since `Edit` requires an exact prior\\n   read).\\n4. Run `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `ty check`, and\\n   `prek run --files <changed>` on the full changed set before committing \u2014\\n   expect the manifest-sync hook to auto-bump patch versions for every\\n   affected plugin's `plugin.json`, same as happened in #3042.\\n5. Re-run the grep one final time and confirm it returns zero matches\\n   repo-wide (excluding `__pycache__`).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Also Found During This Same Investigation Separate\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nInvoking the `dh:work-backlog-item` skill (`/dh:work-backlog-item create -- \\\"...\\\"`)\\nfailed on every attempt with `Shell command failed for pattern \\\"!\\\\`...\\\\`\\\":\\n(eval):1: command not found: ...` \u2014 reproduced even with a minimal\\n`create -- \\\"test minimal\\\"` args string, so it is not an args-escaping issue on\\nthe caller's side. This is why this issue was filed via `gh issue create`\\ndirectly instead of the intended skill workflow. Worth a separate\\ninvestigation into the skill's own template (likely a stray bang-backtick\\nshell-exec pattern in its `SKILL.md` or a referenced workflow file).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b5ea647f6934da72288f5b8f228f024bd18568be3cce129ae8422c4657633d15\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPt2EdA\"}"}